  "description": "Compute batched scaled dot-product attention mapping queries and keys to value projections with optional boolean attention masking.\n\nScaled dot-product attention allows O(1) direct information routing across token pairs.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\operatorname{Attention}(Q, K, V, M) = \\operatorname{softmax}\\left( \\frac{Q K^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}} + M \\right) V\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Compute matrix inner products Q K^T scaled by 1/sqrt(d_k)\n2. Apply optional masking by setting masked positions to large negative values\n3. Apply row-wise softmax normalization and project over Value matrix V\n\n### Returns\nNested list representing attended context tensor.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Implement Scaled Dot-Product Attention\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nNatural language consists of discrete words and symbols arranged in sequential order. To process text with neural networks, we convert words into continuous embedding vectors and model their grammatical and semantic relationships. **Implement Scaled Dot-Product Attention** is a core sequence-processing mechanism used in modern Transformer and LLM architectures.\n\nScaled dot-product attention allows O(1) direct information routing across token pairs. In this problem, the goal is to: compute batched scaled dot-product attention mapping queries and keys to value projections with optional boolean attention masking.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Attention}(Q, K, V, M) = \\operatorname{softmax}\\left( \\frac{Q K^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}} + M \\right) V\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Compute matrix inner products Q K^T scaled by 1/sqrt(d_k)\n2. **Phase 2**: Apply optional masking by setting masked positions to large negative values\n3. **Phase 3**: Apply row-wise softmax normalization and project over Value matrix V\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Self-Attention Mechanics**: Scaled dot-product attention computes all-to-all token interactions dynamically, allowing tokens to gather context from the entire sentence simultaneously.\n* **Position Encodings**: Because self-attention is permutation-invariant, positional encodings (like sinusoidal or Rotary Position Embeddings) inject word order into the representations.\n* **Vocabulary & Subwords**: Algorithms like BPE tokenize text into frequent subwords, allowing models to represent rare words without requiring an infinite vocabulary.",
