  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Implement Scaled Dot-Product Attention** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np, math\n\ndef inference_scaled_dot_product_attention(q: list, k: list, v: list, mask: list = None) -> list:\n    Q, K, V = np.array(q, dtype=np.float64), np.array(k, dtype=np.float64), np.array(v, dtype=np.float64)\n    sc = np.matmul(Q, np.swapaxes(K, -1, -2)) / math.sqrt(Q.shape[-1])\n    if mask is not None: sc = np.where(np.array(mask) == 0, -1e9, sc)\n    ex = np.exp(sc - np.max(sc, axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n    return np.round(np.matmul(ex / np.sum(ex, axis=-1, keepdims=True), V), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
